he unpatched app:\n\n```zsh\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/resonance-sm66-patch/scripts/launch-resonance.sh --check\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/resonance-sm66-patch/scripts/launch-resonance.sh\n```\n\nVerify that the game process remains active and that `AsoboReport-RunningSession.txt` contains an initialized `[Renderer]` section with `EnableD3D12=true`. A process alone is insufficient because the former fatal dialog could leave it waiting.\n\n## Shader or animation corruption\n\nThe shipped game has one gameplay executable and officially requires DirectX 12. The local build imports `D3D11CreateDevice`, but exposes only `D3D12Renderer_Z`; this import is not evidence of a DX11 rendering mode. Do not add an unverified `-dx11` argument.\n\nWhen materials or animations break after the Shader Model patch, inspect the runtime log first. The observed mixed cache contained 766 `.psocache` files, began before the 6.6 patch, and coincided with `AGX: exceeded compiled variants footprint limit`. Quit the game, archive the regenerable PSO cache, and relaunch through the validated launcher:\n\n```zsh\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/resonance-sm66-patch/scripts/reset-resonance-shader-cache.sh --status\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/resonance-sm66-patch/scripts/reset-resonance-shader-cache.sh --reset\n```\n\nThe helper moves the cache into `/Users/zenray/Create/Share/tmp-resonance-shader-cache/`; it never deletes it. The first level load can stutter while the game compiles a clean cache.\n\nRestore the saved original only when requested:\n\n```zsh\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/resonance-sm66-patch/scripts/patch-resonance-sm66.sh restore\n```\n\nIf `status` reports an unknown hash, stop. A game update may have moved the function. Find the error string cross-reference, disassemble the surrounding `CheckFeatureSupport` call and comparison, then update the offsets and hashes from evidence. Never replace every `0x67` in the executable.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"4ab21c77-6b83-4229-bf5f-